{
  "id": "grammar.a1.128.b",
  "title": "Wearing the one you mean",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Visel with a / az",
      "content": "When you mean a particular item, with *a* or *az* in front of it, *visel* takes the definite endings, as *kér* does: *Viselem a fekete sapkát.* (I wear the black hat.) *Anna viseli a kék kabátot.* Answer *Viseled a kék kabátot?* with *Igen, viselem.*"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Present of visel (definite)",
      "rows": [
        [
          "én viselem",
          "I wear it"
        ],
        [
          "te viseled",
          "you wear it"
        ],
        [
          "ő viseli",
          "he / she wears it"
        ],
        [
          "mi viseljük",
          "we wear it"
        ],
        [
          "ti viselitek",
          "you (pl.) wear it"
        ],
        [
          "ők viselik",
          "they wear it"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "title": "Examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Viselem a fekete sapkát.",
          "english": "I wear the black hat."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Anna viseli a kék kabátot.",
          "english": "Anna wears the blue coat."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Viseled a szürke nadrágot?",
          "english": "Do you wear the grey trousers?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Ők viselik a fehér pólókat.",
          "english": "They wear the white T-shirts."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Mi viseljük a barna cipőt.",
          "english": "We wear the brown shoes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Compare *Fekete sapkát viselek* (a black hat, indefinite) with *Viselem a fekete sapkát* (the black hat, definite)."
    }
  ]
}
